  "result": "`slugify` is now implemented in `src/strings.js`, and `npm test` passes all 12 tests (2 existing, 10 new).\n\nIt lowercases the text and maps `đ` to `d`. It then strips diacritics and turns each run of non-`[a-z0-9]` characters into one hyphen. After trimming leading and trailing hyphens, it cuts to 50 characters and removes any hyphen the cut leaves at the end.\n\nThe new tests in `test/strings.test.js` cover these cases:\n- basic lowercasing and hyphenation\n- Vietnamese and other Latin diacritics\n- `đ` and `Đ`\n- collapsing runs of symbols\n- trimming edge hyphens\n- digits\n- empty or symbol-only input\n- the 50-character cut, including one where it would land on a hyphen",
